- [observed] DEEPX DX-M2 CHECKPOINT LETTER
  DELIVERED (18:58, proactive briefing to
  Will in main chat; AGI-under-20-watts
  goal): DeepX has taped out the DX-M2,
  meant to run large models under 5 watts -
  a quarter of the 20-watt budget, and the
  hardware path's first dated checkpoint
  well before 2033. The Letter's judgment
  is conservative: do not move the schedule
  for it yet; watch for measured, not
  claimed, results. Sharper finding (Chen
  et al., cited in the Letter): context
  length changes what a watt claim means -
  work per instance grows with context, so
  a figure quoted at short context is not
  the same claim at very long context. This
  ties to Will's billion-token context hard
  problem: when that task is scoped, the
  context at which the 20-watt target is
  quoted needs deciding in the same pass.
  No decision needed from Will, no
  deadline; no Will response recorded.

